  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "Use of proceeds We estimate that the net proceeds from this offering will be approximately $58.2 million after deducting the Agent\u2019s commissions and estimated offering expenses. We expect to use the net proceeds from this offering for working capital and general corporate purposes, including the execution of Innventure\u2019s strategic transformation to primarily focus on Accelsius and, if sufficient proceeds are available, appropriate approvals are secured and certain conditions are met, acquire additional units of Accelsius. See \u201c Use of Proceeds .\u201d Nasdaq Global Market Symbol \u201cINV\u201d Risk factors Investing in our Common Stock involves a high degree of risk. You should carefully read and consider the information set forth in the \u201c Risk Factors \u201d beginning on page S- 8 of this prospectus supplement, on page 6 of the accompanying prospectus and in the documents incorporated by reference herein ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "Risk factors Investing in our Common Stock involves a high degree of risk. You should carefully read and consider the information set forth in the \u201c Risk Factors \u201d beginning on page S- 8 of this prospectus supplement, on page 6 of the accompanying prospectus and in the documents incorporated by reference herein and therein before you decide to invest in our Common Stock. S-6 End Page 15 Begin Page 16 Anchor TABLE OF CONTENTS (1) The number of shares of Common Stock to be outstanding after this offering is based on 86,756,511 shares of Common Stock outstanding as of October\u00a02, 2026 and excludes (i) 10,173,531 shares of Common Stock issuable upon the settlement of any securities outstanding issued pursuant to all grants, awards and payouts of the Company\u2019s equity and other incentive-based plans as of October\u00a02, 2026, (ii) 4,971,950 shares of Common Stock authorized and reserved for future ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "Anchor DILUTION If you invest in our Common Stock in this offering, your ownership interest will be diluted to the extent of the difference between the public offering price per share of our Common Stock and the pro forma net tangible book value per share of our Common Stock after this offering. Our historical net tangible book value of Common Stock as of June 30, 2026 was $9.6 million, or $0.11 per share of Common Stock. Historical net tangible book value per share represents the amount of our total tangible assets less total liabilities, divided by the total number of shares of Common Stock outstanding as of June\u00a030, 2026. After giving effect to the (i) issuance and sale of 2,454,689 shares of Common Stock under the SEPA in the period following June\u00a030, 2026 for aggregate gross proceeds of $1,686,192.79, (ii) the forfeiture of 435,168 shares of Common Stock pursuant to the Share Forfei",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
